CONCLUSION

The Student Management System serves as a digital transformation tool for educational institutions, replacing traditional paper-based record-keeping with an efficient, centralized platform. By tracking essential academic components—such as students, departments, courses, lecturers, enrollment, attendance, results, and scholarships ,the system delivers three primary benefits.
Enhanced administrative efficiency as it automates routine administrative tasks ,like tracking attendance and ensures data accuracy while making student records easy to access and update.
Improved performance monitoring as it enables institutions to effectively organize student data and closely monitor academic progress and attendance.
Optimized student experience as it empowers students with self-service capabilities, eliminating long office queues, reducing administrative errors, and minimizing operational delays and workloads.
